{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2019-12-06 22:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E SAYS REACHED $13.5 BLN AGREEMENT TO RESOLVE INDIVIDUAL CLAIMS RELATING TO WILDFIRES', 'text': "DEC 6  - PG&E CORP <PCG.N>::IN FINAL MAJOR SETTLEMENT, PG&E REACHES AGREEMENT TO RESOLVE INDIVIDUAL CLAIMS RELATING TO THE 2017 AND 2018 WILDFIRES AND THE 2015 BUTTE FIRE.PG&E ACHIEVES FULLY-FUNDED EQUITY BACKSTOP COMMITMENTS.COMPANY ON PATH TO MAKING MAJOR CHANGES NECESSARY TO EXIT BANKRUPTCY AHEAD OF JUNE 30, 2020, DEADLINE.SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT IS VALUED AT APPROXIMATELY $13.5 BILLION AND HAS SUPPORT OF OFFICIAL COMMITTEE OF TORT CLAIMANTS (TCC).SETTLEMENT WILL RESOLVE ALL CLAIMS ARISING FROM 2017 TUBBS FIRE, CLAIMS FROM 2015 BUTTE FIRE AND 2016 GHOST SHIP FIRE IN OAKLAND.SETTLEMENT IS SUBJECT TO A NUMBER OF CONDITIONS AND IS TO BE IMPLEMENTED PURSUANT TO PG&E'S CHAPTER 11 PLAN OF REORGANIZATION."}